==Russian==

===Etymology===
Compare (with different vocalism) {{cog|uk|му́кати||to [[moo]]}}, {{cog|bg|муча́||to [[moo]]}}, also {{m|bg|му́кам}}, {{cog|sh|му́кати||to [[moo]]}} (1sg. {{m|sh|му̑че̄м}}), {{cog|sl|múkati||to [[moo]]}}, {{cog|cs|mukati||to [[moo]]}}, {{cog|hsb|mučeć||to [[moo]]}}, and more distantly {{cog|lt|mū̃kia||it moos}}, {{cog|grc|μῡκάομαι||to [[moo]], to [[roar]]}}, {{cog|gmh|mūhen||to [[moo]]}}, also {{m|gmh|mugen}}, {{cog|gml|mucken||to be [[quietly]] [[indignant]]}}, {{cog|grc|μυγμός||[[sigh]]}}, {{m|grc|μύζω||to [[groan]], to [[moo]]}}, {{cog|la|mūgiō||to [[moo]]}} (infinitive {{m|la|mūgīre}}), {{cog|sa|मुञ्जति|tr=múñjati||to [[make]] a [[sound]]}}, also {{m|sa|मोजति|tr=mṓjati}}, {{cog|hit|tr=mūgāi-|||to [[lament]], to [[resist]]}}, etc. Ultimately {{onomatopoeic|ru|title=onomatopoeic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|мыча́ть}}

===Verb===
{{ru-verb|мыча́ть|impf|pf=промыча́ть|vn=мыча́ние}}

# to [[moo]]
#: {{ux|ru|чья́ [[бы]] [[коро́ва]] '''мыча́ла''', [[а]] [[твой|твоя́]] [[б]] [[молчать|молча́ла]]|[[pot calling the kettle black]]|lit=other's cow could '''moo''', but yours should better be silent}}
# to [[bellow]]
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} to [[mumble]]

====Conjugation====
{{ru-conj|impf-intr|5b|мыча́ть}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|замыча́ть|g=pf}}
* {{l|ru|помыча́ть|g=pf}}
* {{l|ru|промыча́ть|g=pf}}
''Compounds:''
* {{l|ru|не мыча́ть, не те́литься|g=impf}}

